; regression test: `let` with no arguments used to raise an error message that still said
; "`fix` takes new constants..." -- a leftover from before the keyword was renamed from `fix`
; to `let`. Confirmed the stale wording directly before fixing it. Not a soundness bug (the
; statement is correctly rejected either way, so `expect "EvalError"` alone wouldn't catch a
; regression back to the old wording), just a confusing error message -- caught here by the text
; of the message.
expect "EvalError" "`let` takes new constants or boolean expressions"
    let
